# Android Implementation Roadmap

## Development Phases

### Phase 1: Foundation ✅ (Complete)
- Native Kotlin Android app with Jetpack Compose
- MVVM architecture with ViewModels and StateFlow
- Hilt dependency injection and Material Design 3
- Backend integration with Retrofit and type-safe APIs

### Phase 2: Content System ✅ (Complete)  
- LazyColumn news feed with infinite scrolling
- Content preview cards with source attribution
- Repository pattern with caching strategy
- Feed personalization and filtering

### Phase 3: WebView Integration ✅ (Complete)
- Android WebView with JavaScript bridge
- URL navigation and state management
- Bridge communication testing
- Error handling for WebView operations

### Phase 4: Translation System 🚧 (Current)
- ML Kit Translation API for on-device processing
- JavaScript content extraction and DOM injection
- Translation controls and language selection
- Visual feedback and progress indicators
- End-to-end testing automation

### Phase 5: Advanced Features 📋 (Planned)
- Intelligent content classification
- Context-aware translation with appropriate tone
- Translation quality indicators
- Performance optimization for complex pages

### Phase 6: Production Ready 📋 (Planned)
- Performance optimization and memory management
- Security audit and privacy compliance
- Beta testing and launch preparation

## Key Architecture Decisions

**Technology Choices:**
- Native Kotlin for performance and ML Kit integration
- On-device translation for privacy and offline capability
- WebView with JavaScript bridge for content manipulation
- E2E Appium headless and headed testing

**Success Criteria:**
- Translation works on 80% of tested websites
- Translation response time < 3 seconds
- User engagement: >60% use translation feature
- App performance: startup < 3 seconds